<UpdatePage title="A weekly review that ends with a next step" description="Four questions for turning a busy week into a lesson, a decision and an action." path="/updates/a-weekly-review-with-a-next-step.html">
  <p>A week can be full without moving the thing you care about forward. A short review gives you a chance to notice that before starting another one.</p>
  <p>The <a href="/weekly-review-template.html">template on this site</a> uses four sets of questions. You can answer them on paper or in whatever notes app you already use.</p>
  <h2>1. What happened?</h2>
  <p>Write down what moved forward, what slipped and what surprised you. Keep this factual. A list of what actually happened is more useful than a verdict on whether you had a good week.</p>
  <h2>2. What did you learn?</h2>
  <p>Look for an assumption that changed. Perhaps a task took longer than expected, a conversation answered a question, or something you thought mattered turned out to be unnecessary.</p>
  <h2>3. What matters next?</h2>
  <p>Choose the one outcome that would make next week meaningful. Then ask what you can stop carrying so it has room to happen.</p>
  <h2>4. What will you commit to?</h2>
  <p>Turn the outcome into an action you can schedule. Include room for health and relationships alongside work.</p>
  <h2>An illustrative example</h2>
  <p>Imagine you're making a small website. You spent the week adjusting the design, but you still haven't published the page that explains your project.</p>
  <ul><li><strong>What happened:</strong> the homepage looks better; the project description is still unfinished.</li><li><strong>What I learned:</strong> polishing the layout was easier than deciding what I wanted to say.</li><li><strong>What matters next:</strong> make the project understandable to someone seeing it for the first time.</li><li><strong>What I commit to:</strong> draft the four-sentence explanation on Monday, ask one person to read it, then publish it.</li></ul>
  <p>The review has done its job when it produces a decision you can act on.</p>
  <p><a href="/weekly-review-template.html">Use the weekly-review template →</a></p>
</UpdatePage>
